meta {
  name: Rebuild the knowledge graph
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/graph/rebuild?with_triples=false
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  with_triples: false
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
}

docs {
  Rebuilds the knowledge graph from documents ALREADY ingested — no connector round-trip, no
  re-chunk, no re-embed. Use it when the graph extractors changed but the documents did not:
  a re-sync would re-download everything and re-embed whatever shifted, to reach the same
  edges.

  Starts a background job (source `knowledge graph`); watch it with
  `GET /api/sync/knowledge graph/logs`. 409 while another job is running — it writes edges
  across sources.

  `with_triples=false` (default) rebuilds only the deterministic layer (code structure,
  pub/sub, dependency maps, ticket keys, tables, and the connector's stored payload) and
  needs no LLM. `with_triples=true` also re-queues LLM relationship mining — one model call
  per document, so hours on a large corpus — and 409s when `graph.extract_triples` is off.

  Add `?source_id=azure_devops:TFS` to scope it to one source. Call
  `GET /api/graph/rebuild/preview` first to see how many documents can only be preserved
  rather than rebuilt in full.
}
